    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (72.25) stand out as our elite anchors. **Lawrence Butler** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Brandon Young; the combination of a high-ceiling park factor and a 13% platoon advantage makes him our most efficient start. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** maintains a strong baseline despite a slightly tougher matchup, as his high-leverage spot in the batting order and consistent efficiency ensure he remains our primary engine for counting stats. **JJ Bleday** (64.32) and **Zack Gelof** (63.47) also earn strong starts, with **JJ Bleday** in particular capitalizing on a 14% platoon edge against D. Peterson to offset the moderate SP skill of his opponent.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Braden Montgomery** (45.07). While his score was respectable, the optimizer prioritized the higher-upside profiles of **Dylan Beavers** (60.47) and **Jonathan Aranda** (58.32), the latter of whom gains a massive 12% boost from a platoon advantage against Mize. We have opted to hold **Justin Crawford** and **Luis Arraez** on the bench today, as the matchup against Detmers suppresses their scoring efficiency below our current threshold. Note that while **Bryce Harper**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Dylan Beavers** are currently based on projected lineup spots, we must keep a close watch on official confirmations; should **Jung Hoo Lee** move down the order, his utility as a stolen base threat remains high, but his overall efficiency score will shift.\n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding the heavy rotation of left-handed bats like **Gleyber Torres** and **Daulton Varsho** against skilled arms. **Gleyber Torres** (52.20) sees his score buoyed by an order-based boost, but facing an elite arm in Skubal carries inherent risk. Meanwhile, **Yainer Diaz** (45.46) and **Cal Raleigh** (45.49) sit at the low end of our starting criteria due to high-skill matchups; however, we are starting them to maintain our category floors, as the scarcity of their positions outweighs the marginal risk associated with their sub-50 projections. Keep a close eye on the wind conditions impacting **Jung Hoo Lee**, as any significant change in the forecast could flip his status from a comfortable start to a fringe decision.",
